# Security review ahead of the GCP migration: without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would
# bake the real local .env (Mongo password, JWT_SECRET, ADMIN_TOKEN, ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY,
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY) permanently into the image's filesystem layers — readable by anyone
# with pull access to the Artifact Registry repo, independent of Secret Manager doing the
# right thing for the running container. Runtime config comes from Secret Manager via
# `gcloud run deploy --set-secrets`, never from a file in the image.
.env
.env*
